{#
    The head, once, for both layouts.

    `soul-boot.js` is not a module and loads first: it writes the stored
    choice into `data-theme` before the first paint. Without it the choice
    goes on the next page. It writes nothing where nobody has chosen. The
    machine's setting is what the tokens answer with anyway. An attribute
    that stands in for it is a choice the switch can never step back out of.
#}
<meta charset="utf-8" />
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
{#- The project's name once. On a landing page the two are the same, and
    "Soul Design System — Soul Design System" is a tab nobody wrote. -#}
<title>{{ title }}
    {%- if env.projectNode.title and title != env.projectNode.title %} — {{ env.projectNode.title }}{% endif -%}</title>
{#- The mark in the tab. One `<link>` per file the project configured, and the
    browser picks by the size it needs. That is how a mark drawn at three
    optical sizes reaches the slot it exists for. Written with `asset()` like
    the signet is. So the path resolves from the page in hand, and a page
    below the root reaches the same file. -#}
{%- for icon in soul.favicons %}
<link rel="icon" href="{{ asset('/' ~ icon.href) }}"
      {%- if icon.type %} type="{{ icon.type }}"{% endif %}
      {%- if icon.sizes %} sizes="{{ icon.sizes }}"{% endif %} />
{%- endfor %}
{#- The same document as Markdown, beside the page.

    The renderer writes both. `md` is an output format and a format's name is
    the file extension, so the twin is `<this page>.md`. Every link inside it
    points at the twin of the page it names. The canonical is the other half
    of that pair — it says which of the two representations the document
    *is*. So both stand together or neither does, and a project that turned
    the twin off has one representation and nothing to say about it. -#}
{%- set twin = soul.markdown and env.hasCurrentFileName ? env.currentFileName|split('/')|last : '' %}
{%- if twin %}
<link rel="alternate" type="text/markdown" href="{{ twin }}.md" />
<link rel="canonical" href="{{ twin }}.html" />
{%- endif %}
<script src="{{ root }}styles/soul-boot.js"></script>
{#- The variable faces a page opens in. The preload starts them before the
    stylesheet parses; `font-display: optional` keeps a late response out of
    the fallback's place after paint. Each file covers every used weight. -#}
<link rel="preload" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin
      href="{{ root }}styles/fonts/source-sans-3-latin-wght-normal.woff2" />
<link rel="preload" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin
      href="{{ root }}styles/fonts/source-code-pro-latin-wght-normal.woff2" />
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ root }}styles/soul.css" />
<script type="module" src="{{ root }}styles/soul.js" defer></script>
